IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nlca-dates`
IMPORT `nlca-rules`

-- Limitation Act 1981 (NT), child abuse provisions -- the questions of the SURVIVOR.
--
-- SEAT: the individual against whom child abuse was perpetrated, who brings or proposes to bring an action for damages
-- for the injury it caused -- and, where that person has died, the family member suing under the Compensation (Fatal
-- Injuries) Act 1974 or the person acting for the estate, who stand in the same seat (s 5A(4)). "Was what was done to me
-- child abuse?", "Is there any time limit on my action?", "Can the court still stop my case because it is so old?", "My
-- earlier case was dismissed as out of time, or settled, before 15 June 2017: can I sue now?", "Can the court set the
-- earlier judgment aside, and what will it take into account?". No seat for the defendant, the institution, an insurer or
-- the court: the court's findings are asked as facts.
--
-- Every question takes plain facts (yes/no, dates, a choice from a list) and calls the rules of nlca-rules.l4. No
-- question takes a DEONTIC or an EVENT; the provisions encoded here set no duty with a deadline.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Not an official version of the Limitation Act 1981 (NT). Copyright in Northern Territory legislation is
-- owned by the Northern Territory. Quoted under the Northern Territory copyright policy of 8 October 1996; see
-- SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Limitation Act 1981 (NT): the child abuse survivor's questions`

§§ `Section 5A: no limitation period for child abuse`

@export Was what was done to me "child abuse" under the Limitation Act 1981 (NT) s 5A(6)? It is if it was sexual abuse, serious physical abuse, or psychological abuse arising from either, perpetrated against you while you were under 18.
GIVEN `what was done` IS A `Kind of conduct` @desc What was done to you: sexual abuse; serious physical abuse; psychological abuse; or other harm or ill-treatment
      `did it arise from sexual or serious physical abuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For psychological abuse only: whether it arose from sexual abuse or serious physical abuse (answer no for the other kinds; it does not matter for them)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth (for a death or estate claim, the date of birth of the person who was abused)
      `the day it was done` IS A DATE @desc The day the abuse was perpetrated (if it went on over a time, the day of the act you are asking about)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Was what was done to me child abuse` MEANS
    `s 5A(6) -- it is child abuse` `what was done` `did it arise from sexual or serious physical abuse` `my date of birth` `the day it was done`

@export Is there any time limit on my action for an injury caused by child abuse (Limitation Act 1981 (NT) ss 5, 5A)? For damages for personal injury from child abuse there is no limitation period under this Act: you may sue at any time, however long ago it happened, in tort, contract, under statute or otherwise. The same holds for a family's claim for the death and a claim for the estate. A time limit set by another Act still applies.
GIVEN `what was done` IS A `Kind of conduct` @desc What was done to you: sexual abuse; serious physical abuse; psychological abuse; or other harm or ill-treatment
      `did it arise from sexual or serious physical abuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For psychological abuse only: whether it arose from sexual abuse or serious physical abuse (answer no for the other kinds)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth (for a death or estate claim, the date of birth of the person who was abused)
      `the day it was done` IS A DATE @desc The day the abuse was perpetrated
      `what my action is` IS A `Kind of action` @desc What your action is: your own action for damages for personal injury (in tort, contract, under statute or otherwise); a family's action under the Compensation (Fatal Injuries) Act 1974 for the death of the person abused; an action for that person's estate on a cause of action that survived the death; or an action that is not for damages for personal injury
      `did the injury arise from the abuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the personal injury (or, for a death claim, the death) arose from that abuse
      `does another Act set a time limit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another Act sets a limitation period for this kind of action (if so, the Limitation Act does not apply to it: s 5)
GIVETH AN `Effect of section 5A`
`Is there a time limit on my child abuse action` MEANS
    `s 5A -- the effect on my action` (`s 5A(6) -- it is child abuse` `what was done` `did it arise from sexual or serious physical abuse` `my date of birth` `the day it was done`) `what my action is` `did the injury arise from the abuse` `does another Act set a time limit`

@export Even with no time limit, can the court still dismiss or permanently stay my child abuse action because so much time has passed (Limitation Act 1981 (NT) s 5A(5))? Section 5A does not limit the court's other powers: if the court finds that the lapse of time makes a fair trial impossible, the section does not stop it dismissing or staying the case. Otherwise the Act leaves it to the court.
GIVEN `does section 5A apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your action is one with no limitation period under s 5A (the answer to the time limit question)
      `has the court found a fair trial impossible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has found that the lapse of time has a burdensome effect on the defendant so serious that a fair trial is not possible (the court's finding)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the court still dismiss or stay my action for delay` MEANS
    `s 5A(5) -- the court may still dismiss or stay for delay` `does section 5A apply` `has the court found a fair trial impossible`

§§ `An earlier case before 15 June 2017 (ss 53-55)`

-- Arises only for a person who had an earlier action, judgment or settlement on the claim before 15 June 2017, when the
-- limitation periods for child abuse were removed.

@export My child abuse claim was dismissed as out of time, settled, or still running before 15 June 2017: can I sue now (Limitation Act 1981 (NT) ss 53-55)? Yes despite a judgment or settlement made because the claim was out of time (or a legal professional negligence judgment on that ground), as if the earlier action had not been started; a case still undecided on 15 June 2017 loses its time limit; no where a court finally decided the matter on other grounds before then.
GIVEN `is it a child abuse claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is for damages for personal injury arising from child abuse (the answer to the time limit question)
      `what happened in my earlier case` IS AN `Earlier case` @desc What happened in your earlier case: there was none; a judgment that the limitation period had expired; a judgment on legal professional negligence given on the ground that the limitation period had expired; a judgment finally deciding the matter on other grounds; a settlement agreement made because the claim was out of time; a settlement agreement made for other reasons; or an action you brought that had no judgment by 15 June 2017
      `day of the judgment or settlement` IS A DATE @desc The day the earlier judgment was given or entered, or the settlement agreement was made (any date if there was none)
      `day the earlier action was brought` IS A DATE @desc For an earlier action that had no judgment by 15 June 2017: the day you brought it (any date otherwise)
      `was it a period under the Limitation Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the limitation period in the earlier case was one fixed by the Limitation Act 1981 (NT) or an Act it repealed (rather than by another Act)
GIVETH A `Where my earlier case leaves me`
`Can I sue now after my earlier case` MEANS
    `ss 53-55 -- where my earlier case leaves me` `is it a child abuse claim` `what happened in my earlier case` `day of the judgment or settlement` `day the earlier action was brought` `was it a period under the Limitation Act`

@export Can this court set aside the earlier judgment or settlement that ended my child abuse claim as out of time before 15 June 2017 (Limitation Act 1981 (NT) s 54(5)-(7))? Only if it considers it just and reasonable. The court hearing your new action can; the Supreme Court can also on an application even if it is not hearing it; any other court cannot set aside another court's judgment.
GIVEN `what happened in my earlier case` IS AN `Earlier case` @desc What happened in your earlier case: a judgment that the limitation period had expired; a judgment on legal professional negligence given on that ground; a settlement agreement made because the claim was out of time; or another outcome (a judgment on other grounds, a settlement for other reasons, an action still undecided, or none)
      `day of the judgment or settlement` IS A DATE @desc The day the earlier judgment was given or entered, or the settlement agreement was made
      `which court I am asking` IS A `The court asked` @desc Which court you are asking: the Supreme Court hearing your new action; the Supreme Court on an application, not hearing your action; another court hearing your new action; or another court not hearing it
      `who gave the earlier judgment` IS A `Who gave the earlier judgment` @desc Who gave the earlier judgment: the same court you are asking; a different court; or no court, because it was a settlement agreement
      `does the court consider it just and reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court considers it just and reasonable to set the earlier judgment or settlement aside (the court's judgment)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can this court set aside my earlier judgment or settlement` MEANS
    `s 54(5)(a), (6), (7) -- the court may set aside the earlier judgment` `what happened in my earlier case` `day of the judgment or settlement` `which court I am asking` `who gave the earlier judgment` `does the court consider it just and reasonable`

@export In my new child abuse action, what from my earlier case (ended as out of time before 15 June 2017) may the court take into account (Limitation Act 1981 (NT) s 54(5)(b), (c))? If it considers it just and reasonable, the court hearing your new action may take into account damages paid or payable under the earlier judgment or settlement, and costs paid or payable in the earlier action.
GIVEN `what happened in my earlier case` IS AN `Earlier case` @desc What happened in your earlier case: a judgment that the limitation period had expired; a judgment on legal professional negligence given on that ground; a settlement agreement made because the claim was out of time; or another outcome
      `day of the judgment or settlement` IS A DATE @desc The day the earlier judgment was given or entered, or the settlement agreement was made
      `is the court hearing my new action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court you are asking is the court hearing your new action
      `were damages paid or payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any amount was paid, or is payable, to you by way of damages under the earlier judgment or settlement
      `were costs paid or payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any amount was paid, or is payable, by way of costs (by either side) in connection with the earlier action
      `does the court consider it just and reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court considers it just and reasonable to take them into account (the court's judgment)
GIVETH A MAYBE `What the court may take into account`
`What may the court take into account from my earlier case` MEANS
    `s 54(5)(b), (c) -- what the court may take into account` `what happened in my earlier case` `day of the judgment or settlement` `is the court hearing my new action` `were damages paid or payable` `were costs paid or payable` `does the court consider it just and reasonable`
